Patch: 015-web-search
Reason: `providerTools: ['web_search']` turns the CLI's WebSearch on with the built-ins off: offered by name, let through the PreToolUse hook on the built-ins' path (its intent recorded before it runs), and named in the system prompt's note (WEB_SEARCH_NOTE); the session's model proxy decides what the provider may run; the stand-in Anthropic API can answer with a web search the provider ran (its server_tool_use call, its results, and its searches in usage.server_tool_use)
Upstream: ours
Pins: webSearch: the CLI is offered WebSearch alone and told so, the gate lets it through as a built-in call recorded before it runs (safe to repeat), and still denies every other
Pins: with webSearch on, the CLI's WebSearch runs through the proxy, exactly the recorded tool, booked per search; WebFetch, Bash and every other built-in are still denied
Pins: each web search is booked at Anthropic's rate into the session's cost, streamed and whole, and the cap refuses the next request once searches pass it; another hosted tool is still refused
